# =============================================================================
# The AquariusOS login screen — window manager environment
# =============================================================================
# This file is NOT a shell script. labwc parses it itself, one NAME=value per
# line. A line starting with '#' is a comment; trailing comments are not
# supported.
#
# It is empty on purpose. Everything that matters — XDG_SESSION_TYPE,
# XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, QT_QPA_PLATFORM — is already set by
# /usr/libexec/aquarius-greeter before labwc is started, and labwc passes its
# own environment on to everything it runs. Setting the same variable in two
# places is how the two end up disagreeing.
#
# The one thing worth knowing: the SCREEN SIZE is not set here. labwc has no
# monitor settings in its configuration at all, by design — it expects a program
# to tell it over the standard protocol. /usr/libexec/aquarius-greeter-shell
# does that, with the same helper the desktop uses, just before it starts the
# login screen.
# =============================================================================
